## Change and mathematical scope

This package records a conditional compiler-feasibility target at $C=.0033$ and $C=.0033000005$. It keeps [PR #5565](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/5565)'s paid invoice fixed and hypothetically replaces 145 distinct original rank-nine helper targets per FULL by independent rank-four/rank-five targets, with no additional paid jobs. The complete hypothetical bill is 66726 paid jobs, 15424 targets and rank surplus 760. No physical 145-split word or new kappa is supplied.

Applying the credited weighted-Jensen inequality to the existing rank-one-tail endpoint gives a useful sufficient criterion. With rank-mass weights $w_r=p_r r/P_1$ and $\mu=\sum_r w_r\ln r$, $\ln(c)>\mu$ implies $\gamma_C<\alpha$; if $bB\le P_1$, $\delta\le\gamma_C$. The fixed-offset application includes the explicit correction at the diagnostic point, where $u>C$.

The one fixed tuple is cutoff 12, floor 13, $u=.0033000005$, $\rho=.99985$, tensor power 32768, reserve 1e-6, $\theta=39/40$ and logarithm power 22000. At the tested point:

- raw surplus exceeds .389976323560029949280648;
- gamma is below .999780978737406788178684 and delta below .830893792830358397762175;
- the complete normalized paid bound, including both coefficient-two splitting/completion terms, is below .949537674806338372278839;
- capacity, initial range and shifted exits pass; the least 14e9-grid index is 1185397, with predecessor 1185396 rejected and $H=16595558000000000$.

This changes the earlier fixed 17/18 completion contract. Its scoped obstruction remains valid.

The previous Word RAM archive registration used a standalone `VERIFY.json` as if it were a generic registered research package. Its `inputs` entry was not repository-relative, so the shared planner failed before any selected package replay; changing only that path would then make the generic validator reject this legacy package's non-generic schema.

This maintenance PR preserves the standalone capsule and removes the accidental generic registration:

- rename `VERIFY.json` byte-identically to `STANDALONE-VERIFY.json`;
- update only the standalone `MANIFEST.json` inventory key and its README descriptor reference;
- keep every mathematical source, data file, result, license and attribution byte unchanged;
- leave the shared planner and generic schema gates unchanged.

Validation from the exact current main base `df0137efd35e11b4445734bf612bdd4c7ebc330c`:

- the original current package fails its own integrity check exactly at the stale `VERIFY.json` inventory entry;
- the repaired standalone verifier passes its complete normal replay in 7.6 seconds (8 NTT tests, 65,537 RAM slices, 5,096 butterfly cases and 277 whole-program cases);
- its intentional Python `-O` rejection remains intact;
- all 32 manifest hashes pass after replay;
- the actual planner selects no generic package for this metadata-only change, while shared-control planning completes with 3,353 registered packages and excludes the legacy Word RAM capsule;
- `scripts/research_package.py --changed-since HEAD^ --explain-plan ...` returns an empty replay matrix.

